(1799096, 244690, 45857, '<td valign="top">Love the title, great capture, afraid the microwave is too soft for me, as it will be for most. Its a shame, and really the difference between seeing and photography, since our eyes would instantly adjust focus and make us think we could see both microwave and reflection at the same time. Stiil gets a 8 from me for originality.</td>', 'Love the title, great capture, afraid the microwave is too soft for me, as it will be for most. Its a shame, and really the difference between seeing and photography, since our eyes would instantly adjust focus and make us think we could see both microwave and reflection at the same time. Stiil gets a 8 from me for originality.', '2005-10-20 18:17:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1799098, 244690, 42714, '<td valign="top">Now that''s cute.  Creative way to make use of household objects (and appliances).</td>', 'Now that''s cute.  Creative way to make use of household objects (and appliances).', '2005-10-20 18:17:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1799106, 246304, 42714, '<td valign="top">As a photograph, I think this is wonderful.  As far as the theme, it''s questionable.  The reason I say that isn''t to dismiss your efforts, I can see what you''re going for.  What you might not have considered is that the actual signage is so dominant (sharp red/white contrast, graphics, etc.)  that you really don''t look at the reflection at all.</td>', 'As a photograph, I think this is wonderful.  As far as the theme, it''s questionable.  The reason I say that isn''t to dismiss your efforts, I can see what you''re going for.  What you might not have considered is that the actual signage is so dominant (sharp red/white contrast, graphics, etc.)  that you really don''t look at the reflection at all.', '2005-10-20 18:21:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1799109, 246423, 42714, '<td valign="top">This is just heartwarming.  Great interpretation.  Though I''d be interested inn knowing exactly what that plastic mesh is and if you''re either using some sort of liquid in between or a glue/plastic composite.</td>', 'This is just heartwarming.  Great interpretation.  Though I''d be interested inn knowing exactly what that plastic mesh is and if you''re either using some sort of liquid in between or a glue/plastic composite.', '2005-10-20 18:22:50.000000', NULL, 1),
