(1813837, 246088, 3569, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot, Glad you got a ribbon for it.</td>', 'Wonderful shot, Glad you got a ribbon for it.', '2005-10-26 08:27:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813841, 244353, 3569, '<td valign="top">Very clever shot.  A well deserved ribbon.</td>', 'Very clever shot.  A well deserved ribbon.', '2005-10-26 08:29:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813842, 244379, 10413, '<td valign="top">I was surprised how many thought you used a mirror.  Guess that shows how well you set it up.  Wish it had done better for you.</td>', 'I was surprised how many thought you used a mirror.  Guess that shows how well you set it up.  Wish it had done better for you.', '2005-10-26 08:29:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813845, 244400, 3569, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the kind comments.  This is across the lake from my "Wide Angle" shot.  Such a beautiful morning it was.  Van</td>', 'Thanks for the kind comments.  This is across the lake from my "Wide Angle" shot.  Such a beautiful morning it was.  Van', '2005-10-26 08:31:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813875, 246219, 14620, '<td valign="top">Ha Ha!  Mentor is a very strong word, especially since you''ve blown me out of the water on your first two challenges!! :-)  I''ll sit on a dock for you anytime. :-)  Congratulations Eden!!!</td>', 'Ha Ha!  Mentor is a very strong word, especially since you''ve blown me out of the water on your first two challenges!! :-)  I''ll sit on a dock for you anytime. :-)  Congratulations Eden!!!', '2005-10-26 08:49:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813885, 246022, 29490, '<td valign="top">WooHoo Linda!  Nice photo, the title didn''t even click when I was voting!!  Congrats on the top 21!</td>', 'WooHoo Linda!  Nice photo, the title didn''t even click when I was voting!!  Congrats on the top 21!', '2005-10-26 08:58:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813946, 246022, 15711, '<td valign="top">Great vivid colors.  I like the complementary aspect of them.  I didn''t vote on this one.  With two challenges going on, I can''t seem to get to them all any more.  Nice clear capture!! Congrats on the top 25</td>', 'Great vivid colors.  I like the complementary aspect of them.  I didn''t vote on this one.  With two challenges going on, I can''t seem to get to them all any more.  Nice clear capture!! Congrats on the top 25', '2005-10-26 09:37:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813948, 246263, 35804, '<td valign="top"># 10! It''s so nice to finally see you up at the top!</td>', '# 10! It''s so nice to finally see you up at the top!', '2005-10-26 09:38:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813949, 244395, 24111, '<td valign="top">Goregous! Congrats!</td>', 'Goregous! Congrats!', '2005-10-26 09:38:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813950, 246088, 24111, '<td valign="top">I want to spend christmas right there! Congrats!</td>', 'I want to spend christmas right there! Congrats!', '2005-10-26 09:38:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813951, 244353, 24111, '<td valign="top">wonderfully done! Congrats!</td>', 'wonderfully done! Congrats!', '2005-10-26 09:39:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813972, 244084, 45979, '<td valign="top">Amazing shot.  I like clarity of flowers showing through the drops of water.</td>', 'Amazing shot.  I like clarity of flowers showing through the drops of water.', '2005-10-26 09:48:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813990, 246235, 30817, '<td valign="top">Nancy, I again want to take the time to compliment you on this shot. Reviewing my comment below, the yellow splash of color is, of course, upper left; not what I wrote (I''d be dyslexic, if I weren''t so backward to begin with....)  Now that I have seen your portfolio, I admire this shot even more.  Since you specialize in lighthouses, this was not a case of a passing shot of a random scene that struck you.  It is a well thought out decision for an interpretation of something extremely meaningful to you; which, to me, is the essence of photography.  I am becoming inactive on this site, but will pop back in from time to time to look at your work, among others.  I feel your touch is that good.  I shoot my first lighthouse in January.  I hope I can convey its rusticity and sublime beauty the way you have done time after time.</td>', 'Nancy, I again want to take the time to compliment you on this shot. Reviewing my comment below, the yellow splash of color is, of course, upper left; not what I wrote (I''d be dyslexic, if I weren''t so backward to begin with....)  Now that I have seen your portfolio, I admire this shot even more.  Since you specialize in lighthouses, this was not a case of a passing shot of a random scene that struck you.  It is a well thought out decision for an interpretation of something extremely meaningful to you; which, to me, is the essence of photography.  I am becoming inactive on this site, but will pop back in from time to time to look at your work, among others.  I feel your touch is that good.  I shoot my first lighthouse in January.  I hope I can convey its rusticity and sublime beauty the way you have done time after time.', '2005-10-26 09:56:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1813998, 243946, 42066, '<td valign="top">I like the photo overall, good compostition and colours but i feel the background and sky are a bit dull, i think it needs a bit more post editing. This is just my opinion though, i didnt vote but id say a 6 maybe a 7.</td>', 'I like the photo overall, good compostition and colours but i feel the background and sky are a bit dull, i think it needs a bit more post editing. This is just my opinion though, i didnt vote but id say a 6 maybe a 7.', '2005-10-26 10:00:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814023, 245319, 30817, '<td valign="top">Josh, don''t apologize for your vision.  Learn from any mistakes that you made, but don''t ever back down from what goes into your photographs.  The litter in this scene was part of the reality which made this stand away from the "postcard and calendar" sterility that is often wildly applauded on this site.  As for your title of this piece .... it is yours.  Don''t change what you offer from inside.  It is not for you to recieve your soul from others; but to pass it to those who would like to touch it.</td>', 'Josh, don''t apologize for your vision.  Learn from any mistakes that you made, but don''t ever back down from what goes into your photographs.  The litter in this scene was part of the reality which made this stand away from the "postcard and calendar" sterility that is often wildly applauded on this site.  As for your title of this piece .... it is yours.  Don''t change what you offer from inside.  It is not for you to recieve your soul from others; but to pass it to those who would like to touch it.', '2005-10-26 10:19:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814026, 244379, 44220, '<td valign="top">Man were you robbed, but you fooled a lot of people. I gave it a 9.</td>', 'Man were you robbed, but you fooled a lot of people. I gave it a 9.', '2005-10-26 10:21:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814031, 244353, 16493, '<td valign="top">Congratilations on your personal best and first ribbon.<br/>Like the title fits the challenge and the photo.</td>', 'Congratilations on your personal best and first ribbon.Like the title fits the challenge and the photo.', '2005-10-26 10:22:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814035, 246088, 16493, '<td valign="top">Congratilations on your personal best and first ribbon.</td>', 'Congratilations on your personal best and first ribbon.', '2005-10-26 10:23:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814056, 246037, 46181, '<td valign="top">I shot this picture using my desk lamp and a red light bulb with a cutout piece of paper over it.  So, no, it is not a contact lens. ;) I then stared into the light and tried to position it directly around my pupil...you can see it''s slightly off underneath, but I got it pretty close.  I think this was about the 4th picture of about 10.<br/>Being new to this website, I was unsure of the Basic Editing rules about color treatment.  So, I just left it as red and tried to somehow incorporate it into the title.  Are we able to change the RGB if it is applied to the entire photo?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-26 09:36:15.</i></td>', 'I shot this picture using my desk lamp and a red light bulb with a cutout piece of paper over it.  So, no, it is not a contact lens. ;) I then stared into the light and tried to position it directly around my pupil...you can see it''s slightly off underneath, but I got it pretty close.  I think this was about the 4th picture of about 10.Being new to this website, I was unsure of the Basic Editing rules about color treatment.  So, I just left it as red and tried to somehow incorporate it into the title.  Are we able to change the RGB if it is applied to the entire photo?', '2005-10-26 10:33:28.000000', '2005-10-26 10:36:15.000000', 0),
(1814061, 246347, 30817, '<td valign="top">What a shame that such an extremely well-composed, subtlely exposed image that requires thought, contemplation and interpretation be relegated to the depths of the dregs in a theme contest full of leaves, sunsets and McDonalds buildings!  How tragic when photographers ask no more from their art than to be spoonfed its lighter, brighter components, while rejecting the possibility of pondering extraordinary plausibilities.</td>', 'What a shame that such an extremely well-composed, subtlely exposed image that requires thought, contemplation and interpretation be relegated to the depths of the dregs in a theme contest full of leaves, sunsets and McDonalds buildings!  How tragic when photographers ask no more from their art than to be spoonfed its lighter, brighter components, while rejecting the possibility of pondering extraordinary plausibilities.', '2005-10-26 10:36:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814076, 246219, 18339, '<td valign="top">It just goes to shows what a great teacher you are jenesis:)</td>', 'It just goes to shows what a great teacher you are jenesis:)', '2005-10-26 10:42:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814083, 246263, 24454, '<td valign="top">Adi!!!!!!!  Congratulations not only on one of the most beautiful photos I''ve seen -- but on a top 10 finish!   This is amazing!</td>', 'Adi!!!!!!!  Congratulations not only on one of the most beautiful photos I''ve seen -- but on a top 10 finish!   This is amazing!', '2005-10-26 10:48:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814121, 245954, 30817, '<td valign="top">Tyler, In reference to your "photographer''s comments" above, this image DID do well!  You have a great eye for those things which many others cannot see and therefor need to be shown.  This quality is the essence of a photographer .....certainly not necessarily for a camera owner.  There are many of the latter on this site.  Many who own wonderfully expensive and therefore miraculously accurate recording machines with startlingly clean reproductive capabilities.  But you have something the majority here will never possess .... sensitivity to the profound.  I hope to see your visionary interpretations in the future ... not on the front page here (wouldn''t that be revolutionary!), but in museums and exhibition galleries around the world.  Stay with this art.  You are very special.</td>', 'Tyler, In reference to your "photographer''s comments" above, this image DID do well!  You have a great eye for those things which many others cannot see and therefor need to be shown.  This quality is the essence of a photographer .....certainly not necessarily for a camera owner.  There are many of the latter on this site.  Many who own wonderfully expensive and therefore miraculously accurate recording machines with startlingly clean reproductive capabilities.  But you have something the majority here will never possess .... sensitivity to the profound.  I hope to see your visionary interpretations in the future ... not on the front page here (wouldn''t that be revolutionary!), but in museums and exhibition galleries around the world.  Stay with this art.  You are very special.', '2005-10-26 10:57:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814146, 244353, 27304, '<td valign="top">Virkilega flott! :) til hamingju...!</td>', 'Virkilega flott! :) til hamingju...!', '2005-10-26 11:01:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814190, 243835, 30817, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Tommy 2 Tone:</b></div><hr/><i> Cool reflection but your photo has a line right through the center splitting it in half </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>....and this makes it less of an artistically interpretive photograph? Come on, think for yourself.  No one has a license on what is art!</td>', 'Originally posted by Tommy 2 Tone: Cool reflection but your photo has a line right through the center splitting it in half   ....and this makes it less of an artistically interpretive photograph? Come on, think for yourself.  No one has a license on what is art!', '2005-10-26 11:13:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814236, 244782, 35804, '<td valign="top">I honestly thought this would place a bit higher...but a 15 is still a swanky placement Dad...and this is only your 3rd challenge!  : P</td>', 'I honestly thought this would place a bit higher...but a 15 is still a swanky placement Dad...and this is only your 3rd challenge!  : P', '2005-10-26 11:23:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814240, 246188, 40484, '<td valign="top">Thank you to all who posted comments for me.<br/> <br/>To those who would have like to have seen more at the top, I have posted a recropped version here: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=260663" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=260663</a> . This was still a good score for me and I am happy with it.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-28 12:12:09.</i></td>', 'Thank you to all who posted comments for me. To those who would have like to have seen more at the top, I have posted a recropped version here: //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=260663 . This was still a good score for me and I am happy with it.', '2005-10-26 11:23:45.000000', '2006-01-28 12:12:09.000000', 0),
(1814244, 245641, 24454, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Great finish Dave!!   I actually like the score of your commenters as being more deserving of what score this photo should have received, but 6.1 in a challenge with so many gorgeous photos -- great job!!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow!  Great finish Dave!!   I actually like the score of your commenters as being more deserving of what score this photo should have received, but 6.1 in a challenge with so many gorgeous photos -- great job!!! ', '2005-10-26 11:25:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814301, 245414, 22781, '<td valign="top">If I may be honnest I think this picture just lacks an interesting subject.<br/>You hit the challenge head on, it''s a reflection without mirrors, but you also have to try and capture the intrest of the voters and try to please them with what you are showing them.<br/>Make them want to come back and take another look at it, make them wanting to frame it and hang it in their house.<br/>I''m not saying that it''s a bad photo. Technicaly it''s good, it''s focussed it''s sahrp, but that''s about it. Try to please others is the tip I can give you.<br/> <br/>Hope that helps.</td>', 'If I may be honnest I think this picture just lacks an interesting subject.You hit the challenge head on, it''s a reflection without mirrors, but you also have to try and capture the intrest of the voters and try to please them with what you are showing them.Make them want to come back and take another look at it, make them wanting to frame it and hang it in their house.I''m not saying that it''s a bad photo. Technicaly it''s good, it''s focussed it''s sahrp, but that''s about it. Try to please others is the tip I can give you. Hope that helps.', '2005-10-26 11:40:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1814316, 245954, 26464, '<td valign="top">nice. i would have cropped off wall on left, punched up saturation/contrast a bit, and then i''d give it a chance at top 10-20. <br/></td>', 'nice. i would have cropped off wall on left, punched up saturation/contrast a bit, and then i''d give it a chance at top 10-20. ', '2005-10-26 11:43:02.000000', NULL, 0),
