(1816573, 243894, 45021, '<td valign="top">I loved it and gave it a 9 during voting, I don''t think you should get too wrapped up in your score if it is a shot you really like, take photo''s for yourself and if others like them thats great if they don''t you still like it.</td>', 'I loved it and gave it a 9 during voting, I don''t think you should get too wrapped up in your score if it is a shot you really like, take photo''s for yourself and if others like them thats great if they don''t you still like it.', '2005-10-26 23:23:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1816576, 244560, 21816, '<td valign="top">I thought this photo would of done better than it did! Maybe the light is slightly harsh on the side of her face on my monitor but it''s well done. It''s a shame you couldn''t see the flames. It would of highlighted it well and would of looked good in the reflection. Well done Judi!</td>', 'I thought this photo would of done better than it did! Maybe the light is slightly harsh on the side of her face on my monitor but it''s well done. It''s a shame you couldn''t see the flames. It would of highlighted it well and would of looked good in the reflection. Well done Judi!', '2005-10-26 23:24:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1816584, 245850, 22561, '<td valign="top">This was my first challenge. I want to thank f-32 for making my day! myra, I think if I included the source of the red in this image it would wreck my vision for it...the purpose was to be puzzling...to make people try to figure it out. Elsewhere in the discussions I have read that abstracts don''t do well on this site. However, this image did get a POTD at Photoshowdown.com. My thanks to all who commented.</td>', 'This was my first challenge. I want to thank f-32 for making my day! myra, I think if I included the source of the red in this image it would wreck my vision for it...the purpose was to be puzzling...to make people try to figure it out. Elsewhere in the discussions I have read that abstracts don''t do well on this site. However, this image did get a POTD at Photoshowdown.com. My thanks to all who commented.', '2005-10-26 23:25:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1816726, 244291, 28882, '<td valign="top">interesting, nice contrasts.</td>', 'interesting, nice contrasts.', '2005-10-27 00:02:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1816740, 244605, 44951, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Longreach:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t think your score (or some of the comments received) for this image do it justice.  The kids have been captured at angles, in poses and at distances from the camera to make it very interesting.  This is a great age to photograph - faces are alive, and their eyes tell stories in themselves.  I would possibly have cropped the image down a litte to remove the over exposed regions.  Given the circumstances it may have been impossible, however, playing around with the camera position may have added to the reflection.  I like the image and look forward to your entries to future challenges. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comment.<br/> <br/>My whole family is moving from snap shots to really producing artistic photography.  I''m proud of my wife for getting this shot, because it shows me her eye is developing.  I have to admit we took this in the proper time frame for the challenge, but didn''t take it on purpose.  We just wanted to get in the game, and this worked out nicely.  We''ll submit more with planning and creative thought.  We''d love some comments on some of our portfolio shots.  This site is exciting to us as future (on purpose) photographers because of the great atmosphere created by those who are willing to impart their experience and wisdom.</td>', 'Originally posted by Longreach: I don''t think your score (or some of the comments received) for this image do it justice.  The kids have been captured at angles, in poses and at distances from the camera to make it very interesting.  This is a great age to photograph - faces are alive, and their eyes tell stories in themselves.  I would possibly have cropped the image down a litte to remove the over exposed regions.  Given the circumstances it may have been impossible, however, playing around with the camera position may have added to the reflection.  I like the image and look forward to your entries to future challenges.   Thanks for your comment. My whole family is moving from snap shots to really producing artistic photography.  I''m proud of my wife for getting this shot, because it shows me her eye is developing.  I have to admit we took this in the proper time frame for the challenge, but didn''t take it on purpose.  We just wanted to get in the game, and this worked out nicely.  We''ll submit more with planning and creative thought.  We''d love some comments on some of our portfolio shots.  This site is exciting to us as future (on purpose) photographers because of the great atmosphere created by those who are willing to impart their experience and wisdom.', '2005-10-27 00:06:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1816748, 244395, 28742, '<td valign="top">Looks like Woody went under this time. You''re a monster. ;-) <br/>Congrats!</td>', 'Looks like Woody went under this time. You''re a monster. ;-) Congrats!', '2005-10-27 00:09:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1816878, 243894, 34659, '<td valign="top">I scored this a 9 and tend to agree with havy2008.  If you like the shot - enjoy it...  I know I did - and do!  I think it''s GREAT!</td>', 'I scored this a 9 and tend to agree with havy2008.  If you like the shot - enjoy it...  I know I did - and do!  I think it''s GREAT!', '2005-10-27 00:44:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1817166, 245348, 46144, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mosesm:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks like you had potential with this image, just can''t see a reflection in the water though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you, this was my first time, and I wasnt sure if it really fit the "reflection" theme, but wanted to try anyway, and see what people had to say.</td>', 'Originally posted by mosesm: Looks like you had potential with this image, just can''t see a reflection in the water though.   Thank you, this was my first time, and I wasnt sure if it really fit the "reflection" theme, but wanted to try anyway, and see what people had to say.', '2005-10-27 03:13:08.000000', NULL, 0),
