(2112689, 244892, 43019, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rswank:</b></div><hr/><i> By definition it is not a reflection as no light is bouncing off of the object.<br/>The shadow exists by virtue of the object interrupting light. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If light doesn''t bounce off the object, how does the shadow come about? I disagree with your comment. I am not a professional photographer, nor do I take these challenges as seriously as most. Thanks for your comment though.</td>', 'Originally posted by rswank: By definition it is not a reflection as no light is bouncing off of the object.The shadow exists by virtue of the object interrupting light.   If light doesn''t bounce off the object, how does the shadow come about? I disagree with your comment. I am not a professional photographer, nor do I take these challenges as seriously as most. Thanks for your comment though.', '2006-02-01 22:20:03.000000', NULL, 0),
